From 3de78751408ed7350c4f6d726775267571fcfd5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:39:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/27] Port the Wi-Fi (Nintendo WFC) path from ROCKNIXDS
 cursor/drastic-wfc-dns into SuperDrastic

Ported, unchanged in logic, from ROCKNIXDS commit b1a4564 (branch origin/cursor/drastic-wfc-dns-24ad,
written against the old in-repo dsflip/ tree):
- src/wifi.c: replaces DraStic r2.5.2.2's wifi load/store handler tables (BuildID
  7a5e0e5fc6e52e6e8f5499c3d4d667ef51db0748) from a constructor(102), emulates an open access point
  ("rocknixds"), queues 802.11 frames into DraStic's wifi RAM and raises the ARM7 wifi IRQ.
  A "dsf-wfc" service thread (10 ms) drives beacons, the TSF compare and the NAT sockets.
- src/wififrame.c/.h: beacon, probe/auth/assoc responses, from-DS data frames, the RX ring.
- src/wfcnet.c/.h: userspace NAT (DHCP with the chosen DNS, ARP, ICMP echo, UDP NAT, client TCP NAT).
- tools/wfc_test.c: host test for wififrame/wfcnet (`sh build.sh wfc_test`).

Adaptations:
- build.sh: the three sources in SRCS; a `build.sh wfc_test` target (gcc on the build machine).
- wifi.c: constructor(102) runs after dsflip.c's init_locks (101) and before its init() (no
  priority), so it returns early when DSFLIP_IN_GAME is already set (DraStic's `sh -c pactl`
  children inherit the preload, as init() handles).
- wifi.c setting lookup: DSFLIP_WFC (off | kaeru | altwfc | wiilink | <dotted ip>) wins; then
  ROCKNIX's per-game key nds["<rom>.nds"].wfc_dns in system.cfg (the branch looked for a
  configs/nds/<rom>.cfg file that ROCKNIX does not write); then nds.wfc_dns there.
- dsflip_log and dsflip_toast(l1, l2, accent, ms) exist in src/dsflip.c with the same
  signatures the branch used, so no wrapper was needed.
- docs/INTEGRATION.md, tools/README.md: the setting and the test.

Verified: host test passes (wfc_test ok); aarch64 cross-build of libsuperdrastic.so succeeds
with no warnings from the new files (-Wall -Wextra).

Untested: everything on a handheld. The DraStic offsets (handler tables, register and RAM
bases, the ARM7 state block and its IO/IRQ fields), the IRQ delivery from another thread,
and whether DraStic's stock store handler for W_IF is a plain store (the hook assumes it is)
have never been exercised. No DS game has connected through this.

