From d8291e0d67a1a77942bc6ea7dabb2cd5b90e5a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:07:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/27] Microphone: tunables and logs for the handheld, a
 joystick-button fallback for the fake microphone; 0.4.0-beta.2-rocknixds.3

A real blow does nothing on the RG DS (ROCKNIXDS issue 26). The mic thread can now be tuned and watched without a
rebuild: DSFLIP_MIC_DEBUG prints the level, floor, speaker level, learned leak, the gate's bar and the key's state
every ~190 ms and on every press and release; DSFLIP_MIC_GATE sets the echo gate's factor (0 turns it off);
DSFLIP_MIC_COUPLING_MAX caps the leak it learns; DSFLIP_MIC_HOLD_MS keeps the key down for a minimum time.

DSFLIP_MIC_LF asks a press for a low-frequency share (the RMS below ~250 Hz over the RMS) above a value: a blow into
the mic is wind, mostly below that, game sound mostly above. The uploaded logs of an RG DS Plus show the speaker's
leak at the mic (0.2-0.35 RMS) as loud as a blow, where no level bar can tell them apart. Off by default; the 10 s
line reports the share's range over the blocks above floor + threshold so a device run can pick the value.

The thread reads how config/drastic.cfg binds DraStic's fake microphone (resume_control_code) and says so at start:
the keyboard set (327, Scroll Lock) is what we press; when it is unbound but the joystick set has a button, it presses
that button instead (dsflip_mic_button, an SDL_JOYBUTTON event with the joystick DraStic opened), DSFLIP_MIC_KEY picks.
A capture that stays at zero for 5 s is reported as silent (no source behind ALSA's default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
