From fe2c56f1a6a455a5c776ac5dbdf15c6c92678f81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:54:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/27] Stall watch, a quit that works on a stuck game,
 RetroAchievements logins that survive no network

2026-10-05, an RG DS Plus: Black 2 started with its resume state, DraStic stopped presenting frames a few seconds
later and the handheld needed a hard reset. Nothing could end that game: the exit hotkey (resume on quit) only
asks DraStic's main thread to save at its next frame, which never came, and a second press did not escalate;
session.sh's check covers only a SIGKILL the kernel can't deliver.

- dsflip.c: the presenter watches for frames. 5 s without one, outside DraStic's own menu, the in-game menu and
  the quit's save: every thread's state, CPU time, allowed CPUs, syscall, wait channel and kernel stack go to the
  log (fsync'd), a card says the game stopped responding, and the exit hotkey quits at once. 20 s
  (DSFLIP_STALL_QUIT; 0: never): the game is ended, with a line for the launcher's notice (DSFLIP_NOTICE).
- dsflip.c: new threads start on every CPU instead of inheriting their creator's. The RG DS Plus's CPU placement
  confines DraStic's main thread to CPU 3, and threads created from it after that (a state load, the 3D pool)
  shared that one CPU: the deadlock 68dfccd (ROCKNIXDS) saw at start, helpers that never ran and a main thread
  waiting for them. DSFLIP_SPREAD_THREADS=0: inherit as before.
- resume.c: a second exit hotkey press a second or more after the first, a stalled game, or a request DraStic
  doesn't take within 3 s (5 s with the in-game menu up) quits at once, without the resume state.
- ra.c: a request that got no answer passes curl's error to rcheevos (the log and the pop-up said "Login failed: "
  with nothing after it) and logs it with the API name; other HTTP statuses are logged. A login with no answer, a
  429 or a 5xx keeps the saved token and is tried again at 15 s, 30 s, 60 s, then every 2 minutes (it deleted the
  token and tried the password at once, which failed the same way). No empty pop-up lines.

