From af8944a5025f94ff74c9a99bd43b3c0c45401054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:22:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/27] In-game menu: each slot keeps its own picture, both
 screens behind L / R, "LAST" on this session's save (issue 4)

The pictures all showed the same scene after a restart with a resume state (SuperDrastic issue 4). The menu read the
slot files through SuperDrastic's own fopen (resume.c), which points every <game>_<n>.dss at the state being loaded
while a load runs: the resume load at a game's start (2 s in, for 2.5 s) or one of the menu's own. A menu opened then
read the resume state's picture for all eight slots, and the cache, keyed by the files' times, kept them for the rest
of the session. The pictures are now read with libc's fopen, the cache also checks the file's size and inode, and the
menu button does nothing until the resume state is in.

The picture reader checks the header's flags (byte 0x24 of DraStic r2.5.2.2's header: bit 0 compressed, bit 1 a
snapshot first; its save_state copies both screens there, 98,304 bytes each) and reads uncompressed states too, and
keeps both screens: L or R on the Save and Load pages switch every picture between the top and the bottom screen
(Phantom Hourglass plays on the bottom one).

"LAST" (and the main page's "last: slot N") is the slot saved to this session once there is one, instead of the
newest file time only: a save whose file time is older than another slot's (a clock set back) no longer leaves the
label on the slot that was newest when the game started.

