Subject: [PATCH 17/27] In-game menu: a brightness slider per screen, menu
 sounds and tips switches, tips shown only the first times

Quick settings (ROCKNIXDS issue 49, SuperDrastic issue 5):
- Top screen / Bottom screen brightness, each on its own panel, where ROCKNIX's brightness script addresses them
  separately (two /sys/class/backlight entries: "brightness set <n> <pct>", settings display.brightness and
  display.brightness2). The top panel is the screen numbered like DSFLIP_TOP's connector (DSI-2 = dsi1 = backlight1
  = screen 2 on the RG DS, whose device tree pairs backlight0 with dsi0 and backlight1 with dsi1), or
  DSFLIP_BACKLIGHT_TOP=<n>. Anything else keeps the one slider for both.
- Menu sounds On / Off: the menu's navigation sounds. Starts from DSFLIP_MENU_SOUNDS (default 1; ROCKNIXDS sets it from
  ES's navigation sounds).
- Tips On / Off: the tutorial toasts. Starts from DSFLIP_MENU_HINTS (default 1).
- The page scrolls once it has more rows than fit (a bar on the right shows where).

The menu keeps its own settings in <DSFLIP_DATA>/menu.cfg. A switch flipped in the menu holds until the environment's
value changes (the frontend's setting was changed after it), which then wins again.

Tips: "Resumed where you left off" shows the first three resumes only (it came at every start), and the undo tip after
a load the first three loads, worded for where Y works: "Wrong one? Open Load and press Y to undo". Neither shows with
the tips off.

Picking "DraStic menu" no longer brings up the time and battery card that DraStic's menu shows when it opens: the
in-game menu's top screen had both already.

