From 83b4e44fdafd2e3760577f53a5caa78e3957dc06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:25:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/27] Volume keys: the brightness indicator when the function
 key changes the brightness, the top clock while in use

The same keys with ROCKNIX's function key held change the brightness (input_sense), and the indicator showed the volume,
unchanged, meanwhile (ROCKNIXDS issue 49). volume.c now follows display.brightness as well and shows whichever setting
the press changed, with a sun for the brightness (ui_brightness); nothing shows until one of them has changed, or for
400 ms (a press at the end of the scale changes nothing). The settings are read every 50 ms instead of 100 while a
key is in use.

Quick volume presses stuttered the game's sound and changed the volume seconds late, while the menu's slider was fine
(issue 49). Every press, and every 100 ms of a held key, runs ROCKNIX's volume script in new processes (a shell,
pactl, sed on system.cfg), which SuperDrastic's CPU governor doesn't see: at the low clock it had settled on for the
game they took their time from DraStic's threads and PipeWire's. The menu's slider runs the same script, but with the
game and its sound paused. The volume keys now boost the CPU to its top clock for as long as they are in use (as a
savestate does); the governor's windows meanwhile don't count. The process per press is ROCKNIX's.

