 the in-game menu's Quick settings (issue 5)

A few lines of 3x5 pixel text in the top screen's top-left corner, drawn into DraStic's finished top frame in
SDL_RenderPresent before it is queued or shaded: no plane, no thread, a few thousand pixel writes a frame (2x the
size on DraStic's 512x384 hi-res frames). The numbers are taken once a second:
- FPS: the new frames the top panel showed in the last second.
- Detailed: + DraStic's frame time (the average and the longest gap between its presents) and the frames dropped in
  the last second (any cause: replaced before shading, queue overflow, no buffer).
- Advanced: + the CPU's clock (cpufreq policy0), the GPU's (the first devfreq *gpu*) and the internal resolution
  (1x / 2x from DraStic's screen texture; 3x with Gengis Engine at DSFLIP_RAST_SCALE=3).

The choice is kept in <DSFLIP_DATA>/menu.cfg (perf) and applies from the next session's first frame. Nothing is drawn
while the menu holds DraStic's frames back (a load behind the "Loading" screen).

