From 401193342f4e2f7ae7da93db25e9e971302a24c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:34:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/27] Microphone: the capture's DC offset out, a leak the
 echo gate can't talk itself into, the sample pressed again (issue 26)

A real blow did nothing while the menu's Blow worked (ROCKNIXDS issue 26; 1.6.1's known issue: the echo gate held its
bar above any blow). Three defects in the gate's arithmetic:
- No DC removal: a constant offset in the capture counted in every block's RMS, so a blow rose less above the floor
  (sqrt(dc^2 + blow^2) - dc) and the offset went into the leak the gate learns (level / output). A one-pole high-pass
  at ~14 Hz now takes it out before anything is measured (a blow's wind is far above that); the 10 s log line has the
  offset ("dc").
- The leak was learned from the whole level, the room's noise included: with the game quiet, noise over a small
  output read as a leak of x1 and more. It is now learned from the level above the noise floor.
- Every block not pressed was learned from, a blow that stayed under the bar included: each such block raised the
  leak, so the bar climbed during the very blow it should have let through. Blocks above 1.5x the expected leak (plus
  the threshold) no longer teach it, once it has its first 50.

And two in how the fake microphone is pressed. DraStic r2.5.2.2 plays its sample (microphone/<game>.wav, else
microphone.wav, read once at the game's start) from the beginning at each press and gives silence after its end
however long the key stays down (spu_fake_microphone_start keeps the press time; spu_get_microphone_sample returns 0
past the end; with no sample it gives noise for as long as the key is held):
- A blow wavers around the bar, and each release and press restarted the sample: the game heard its first few ms over
  and over. Once pressed, the key now stays down while the level is above 60% of the way from the floor to the bar,
  and at least DSFLIP_MIC_HOLD_MS (now 120 ms by default; was 0).
- A blow held longer than the sample is pressed again at its end (dsflip_mic_restart: release, a barrier that ends
  DraStic's event loop, press), for the real mic and the menu's Blow alike; the sample's length is read from the same
  file DraStic loads.

The menu's Microphone page picks the Blow's length with left / right: 1, 3 (the default) or 10 s, the long one for a
sustained blow (Phantom Hourglass's candles). A louder "shout" can't be switched while the game runs: DraStic reads its
sample once, at the game's start; a louder microphone/<game>.wav in DraStic's folder is the way.

Not measured on a handheld (none here): the defaults are reasoned from the code and the 1.6.1 notes, and
DSFLIP_MIC_DEBUG=1 logs everything needed to check them.

