From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:35:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] Exit combos: held 0.3 s instead of 0.5, and the quit's
 save at the top clock from the first moment (issue 3)

Start + Select took about 8 s back to the menu (SuperDrastic issue 3). What is SuperDrastic's in that: the hold, now
300 ms (was 500), and the resume save. DraStic writes the state on its main thread and compresses it on another; the
CPU boost came only once DraStic opened its temp file, so the press itself and the first frame ran at whatever low
clock the governor had settled on. The quit now boosts as it presses Save. The rest of that wait is outside the
library: ~0.8 s for the save (measured in 1.5), then the frontend's return (on ROCKNIXDS 1.6 the menu is back ~1.2 s
after the hotkey; the 3 s fade the issue saw was the frontend's).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBVcHtDJUrUv4eL8Vsmzy9
