From 5f5b92ce5443cc73dfeab099b9683ccaa899449c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:45:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] 3x: DraStic's edge marking gap passes leave the rows
 the bins wrote (ROCKNIXDS issue 47)

With edge marking on, update_frame_3d_4x re-marks rows 32k-1 and 32k of the output frame after all bins (the gap
passes, spec/resolve.c), from gap buffers that only DraStic's own bin resolve fills. hr.c never wrote them, so at 3x
every bin boundary got two rows of zeros or a 2x frame's leftovers: the black (or purple) lines every 32 rows in the
Zelda games and Dragon Quest IX, gone with "Disable edge marking", which skips those passes. Each 3x bin now fills
its half of the gap buffers with its own output rows and all-zero attributes, which make both the edge and the fog
passes an identity (no bit 30, so no edge colour; no fog flag, so no fog).

RAST_HRCHECK=1 (needs the compositor table, RAST_COMP=2, the default) compares each bin's rows 0 and 31 with the
frame after update_frame_3d_4x returns. The fog and edge-marking scene S4 at 3x: 22 rows changed in every frame
before (299 of 300 frames), 0 after, also with threaded_3d=1 and with disable_edge_marking=1. regress.sh's 3x runs
check it; the 2x checks pass with their known counts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBVcHtDJUrUv4eL8Vsmzy9
