From c2cc3a73ec97ae9f537242a14235c10cac7fbebd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:45:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] 3x: a bin also renders its neighbours' polygons;
 "Disable edge marking" turns the 3x edge marking off

DraStic bins polygons by their 2x lines (bins ytop >> 5 to (ybot - 1) >> 5), but the 3x coordinates are rounded on
their own: a polygon whose 2x lines end at 32k can still cover 3x line 48k, the first line of bin k, and the edge
marking reads the lines just above and below the bin (48k - 1, 48k + 48), where polygons of bin k - 1 or k + 1 alone
may lie. With the bin's own list such a line had holes in the clear colour (and false edges) wherever a row of
vertices sits on a bin boundary: a line across the screen that comes and goes as the scene moves (ROCKNIXDS issue 47:
the flickering line while walking in HeartGold at 3x with edge marking disabled). hr_lists now gives a bin its
neighbours' polygons as well, in DraStic's order: every list is the frame's one polygon sequence filtered by bin,
sorted by the 2x bottom line (video_3d_bin_polygons_y_sort_4x), so the sequence is (k-1 without k) (k without k+1)
(k+1); translucent polygons with manual sorting are in index order and merged. hr_polygon drops a neighbour's
polygon that cannot reach the bin's lines before the walk.

A/B on the field scene S7 at 3x (RAST_DUMP every 30 frames): 10 of 69 frames differ, only in 3x rows 192, 240 and 384
(48k), up to 699 of 768 pixels a row, where the bin's own list left the clear colour. RAST_HRCHECK counts the
neighbours' polygons that drew lines: S7 2910 on a bin's own lines in 3300 frames, L4 3960 in 900.

The 3x resolve ignored DraStic's disable_edge_marking (render context byte CTX_NO_EDGE, which rast.c's 2x resolve
honours): it now skips the edge marking as the 2x path does.

